    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a1">

                <pb facs="0507" n="465" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg465"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 25,1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I had the honor to receive your letter of
                    the 3d instant, enclosing one, with accompanying papers, addressed to you by Mr.
                    Stuart, her Britannic Majesty’s charge d’affaires, in reference to the capture
                    of the steamer Sunbeam, and called upon Commander Armstrong for an explanation
                    in the case. Copies of his report, dated the 15th instant, and accompanying
                    statements, are herewith transmitted.</p>
                <p>I am, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
